1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:06,054
It's a haunted house you run through on live television.
The build says it isn't the same house twice.

2
00:00:06,304 --> 00:00:08,178
It ships a dungeon generator.

3
00:00:10,428 --> 00:00:17,056
Haunted House Hellshift. You collect eyeballs to open cursed doors,
and a studio audience watches.

4
00:00:17,306 --> 00:00:22,524
Two point one gigabytes, Unity on Mono.
So every package name is readable.

5
00:00:22,774 --> 00:00:29,533
And in that list is DunGen — a procedural level builder.
Rooms and rules in, a layout out, at runtime.

6
00:00:29,783 --> 00:00:35,210
So tonight's house isn't the one you learned yesterday.
A design decision, read off a file list.

7
00:00:35,610 --> 00:00:41,220
Worth a dip, and there's local two-player.
Every demo I open, I read the file list first.
